sdk/

# `documents/` is internal working material — cycle plans, vision drafts,
# adopter upgrade notes, investor prep, compliance submission templates. It
# describes HOW axon is built, cycle by cycle, and it is NOT part of the public
# surface. Files stay on disk locally; this rule keeps them out of git.
#
# A FLAT ignore, deliberately: the rule it replaces was `/docs/*` plus an
# `!/docs/papers/` exception, and an exception is a thing you have to remember
# to maintain — one new public folder under the ignored tree and it silently
# never ships. Nothing under `documents/` is public, so nothing needs an escape
# hatch.
#
# The two directories this replaces (`docs/fase/`, `docs/vision/`) are gone:
# `docs/` now means the OPPOSITE. See the note below.
/documents/

# `docs/` and `papers/` are PUBLIC by definition and are NOT ignored:
#   - `docs/`   — the adopter documentation site (docs.ricardovelit.com).
#   - `papers/` — the academic papers the compiler's own gates read
#                 (`the_paper_matches_the_compiler.rs` includes one at compile
#                 time), linked from the README.
#
# Because `docs/` used to hold the internal material, muscle memory is a real
# hazard: a cycle plan written to `docs/fase/` would now be COMMITTED and
# PUBLISHED. A gitignore cannot warn about that — it is silent by construction —
# so the rule is enforced loudly by a test instead
# (`axon-rs/tests/the_public_docs_tree_is_public.rs`), which also fails if this
# `/documents/` line is ever removed.

# §Fase 117.b — the founder's working file, kept at the repo root. It is not
# part of the public surface and must never be committed; ignoring it also
# stops it from sitting in `git status` as a standing invitation to `git add -A`.
pagesapi.html
